    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0299" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1946v05/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.811/11–2146: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Erhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-11-21T19:00:00-05:00">November 21, 1946—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1026. ReDeptel cir 1610 Nov 7,<anchor n="91" xml:id="d183-f1"/> WX 85902 Nov 20
                    to OMGUS and USFA<anchor n="92" xml:id="d183-f2"/> requests US military
                    authorities to discuss with proper <pb facs="0300" n="282" xml:id="pg282"/>
                    Austrian authorities means of returning Austrian Danube vessels to Austrian Govt
                    under circumstances permitting utilization by Austrians in international
                    traffic. Suggestion has been made that formation new Austrian shipping company
                    might safeguard vessels now in US zones from Soviet seizure in operations below
                    Linz.</p>
                <p>Sent Vienna, repeated 2324 to Berlin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
